ld have chimneys that we find perform the transformation of smoke into a liquid that we benefit from, and even the water used in the world’s factories, we do not dispose of it in rivers, but rather treat it and benefit from it by chemical methods.\nWe can appreciate and evaluate these writings by their effectiveness in serving the climate crisis and global warming.\n\n\nDo not ask for any honor or appreciation. A person who does these things by inventing them deserves all appreciation, respect, and honor. The Imam is a scholar. I can explain everything written. I just need a translator to translate the language to explain his idea. Thank you very much, and I am grateful.\n\nPeace be upon you. There are smoke extraction devices used in homes, kitchens, and restaurants. Why not add a feature to convert cooking smoke, whether from homes or restaurants, into a liquid and store it in an inconspicuous place, out of reach of children? If possible, this liquid could be utilized and disposed of safely, avoiding dumping it into the soil to prevent soil contamination or groundwater pollution. I can explain all of this if requested.\n\nAnd now, factories worldwide...\n\nPeace be upon you. Is it possible to convert factory smoke into a liquid before it exits the chimneys, separating the liquid into usable substances? Even the water used in factories, instead of being discarded and damaging the land or contaminating groundwater, could be separated and used for other purposes. If we could do this, we would contribute to preventing global warming and climate change, and we could integrate solar energy into everything instead of electricity, creating a harmonious system where it\'s undetectable as solar-powered, both inside and out. Thank you very much. And gratitude \n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPeace be upon you. It is possible to have the idea of ​​stopping the world\'s forest fires, but I am not good at English, but I will send a translation from Arabic to English using Google Translate. You can also seek help from someone who knows Arabic and English fluently to know the content of this email. The email is\n\nPeace be upon you. The world is witnessing forest fires. If this method works, there will be a glimmer of hope, and we can avoid what the world will suffer if we don\'t act on this. The method is: why not create buffer zones between areas? For example, a buffer zone of barren land with no trees. To illustrate, for instance, between every four kilometers wide and four kilometers long, there would be a buffer zone of barren land with no vegetation. When fires break out, the fires cannot spread beyond this barren land. This way, we contain the fires, preventing losses to the economy, oxygen, and lives. Firefighters who work to extinguish fires might also pay with their lives. I can explain this on paper if asked. I just need a pen, ruler, and paper to explain, but without revealing who suggested this idea. If it works, I would be very grateful. A substance could be applied to prevent fires from spreading across this barren land. I can explain all of this on paper.\n\nPeace be upon you. The world is witnessing forest fires. If this method works, there will be a glimmer of hope and we will avoid what the world will suffer if we do not take action for this thing. The method is: Why are there no partitions made between the forests? In the sense of the partition, a barren land on which there is no tree plantation, as an example, just to explain, between each area, four kilometers in width. And four kilometers in length, between them there is a separator of barren land with no crops on it, and when fires occurred in barren land, fires could not pass over them. Thus, we were besieged by fires, instead of there being losses to the economy, oxygen, people, and also the firefighters. Those who work to extinguish may pay with their lives. Therefore, I can explain on a piece of paper if I am asked to do so. I only need it. A pen, a ruler, and a piece of paper to explain, but without knowing anyone who suggested this idea, if it is useful, many thanks and gratitude to you. A material can be put in place that prevents fires from going through\nOn this barren land, I can explain it all on a piece of paper\n\n\n___________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________\n\nPeace be upon you. The idea is to invest one trillion dirhams per country from its budget, which can be calculated in local currency. This money would be invested in global stocks and commodities under the supervision of each country individually to prevent theft or corruption. The funds would then be used to provide free healthcare, free education, and some free humanitarian aid, which could be identified through cooperation and addressing humanitarian problems. The money previously allocated to education and healthcare would then be used for other purposes.\n\nIt involves some family outings and travel, and perhaps if a solar-powered car were invented, no one would walk long distances. As an official body, you can assess the potential success of this idea. Thank you very much.', 'السلام عليكم لقد قمت ببحث بسيط في جوجل فعرفت هذه المعلومة بأن عدد أيتام العالم سيتجاوز ١٥٠مليون يتيم ويمكنكم معرفة من مصادر موثوقه الفكرة الانسانية بخدمة ليس أيتام العالم فقط إنما خدمة إنسانية في كل دولة على حده وحتى الايتام لكل دولة على حده وغيرها من الاعمال الانسانية لكل دولة على حده يمكننا بمساعدة ضباط بمهب الريح والمختصين والخبراء على مستوى العالم وحتى ناس الذين لهم شأن وناس الذين لهم حماس لاجل إنجاح  بهذا العمل الانساني لاجل إنجاح بمثل هذا الفكرة على مستوى العالم وشخص الذي يحقق هذا شيء يستحق كل تقدير والاحترام وتتويج أمام العالم بالنسبة لي يكفيني أن تؤدي هذه الفكرة غرضها الانساني ملاحظة لا أجيد الانجليزية أستخدم مترجم جوجل للتواصل معكم لا أحب ظهور في وسائل تواصل الاجتماعي ولا اعلام اعتبار هذه الفكرة من فاعل خير الفكرة المعنية بايتام العال