 will send a translation from Arabic to English using Google Translate. You can also seek help from someone who knows Arabic and English fluently to know the content of this email. The email is\n\nPeace be upon you. The world is witnessing forest fires. If this method works, there will be a glimmer of hope, and we can avoid what the world will suffer if we don\'t act on this. The method is: why not create buffer zones between areas? For example, a buffer zone of barren land with no trees. To illustrate, for instance, between every four kilometers wide and four kilometers long, there would be a buffer zone of barren land with no vegetation. When fires break out, the fires cannot spread beyond this barren land. This way, we contain the fires, preventing losses to the economy, oxygen, and lives. Firefighters who work to extinguish fires might also pay with their lives. I can explain this on paper if asked. I just need a pen, ruler, and paper to explain, but without revealing who suggested this idea. If it works, I would be very grateful. A substance could be applied to prevent fires from spreading across this barren land. I can explain all of this on paper.\n\nPeace be upon you. The world is witnessing forest fires. If this method works, there will be a glimmer of hope and we will avoid what the world will suffer if we do not take action for this thing. The method is: Why are there no partitions made between the forests? In the sense of the partition, a barren land on which there is no tree plantation, as an example, just to explain, between each area, four kilometers in width. And four kilometers in length, between them there is a separator of barren land with no crops on it, and when fires occurred in barren land, fires could not pass over them. Thus, we were besieged by fires, instead of there being losses to the economy, oxygen, people, and also the firefighters. Those who work to extinguish may pay with their lives. Therefore, I can explain on a piece of paper if 